      "raw_html": "<div class=\"question\" id=\"question-125323\"><div class=\"questionHeader\"><span class=\"questionNumber\">5.</span><a class=\"questionKP\" href=\"/topics/340#750\">Finding the First Few Terms of the Maclaurin Series of a Function</a><span class=\"helpButton\" questionid=\"125323\">?</span></div><div class=\"questionText\"><p>Find the first three non-zero terms of the Maclaurin expansion of the function <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"481\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\"><mjx-math aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"MJX-TEX\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D453 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c28\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D465 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c29\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c3D\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D465 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-msup><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: 0.363em;\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\" size=\"s\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D465 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-script></mjx-msup><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2E\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml display=\"inline\" unselectable=\"on\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></msup><mo>.</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></p>\n</div><div class=\"answerDetails\"><div class=\"questionDifficulty difficultyHard\">H</div><span class=\"answerCreated\">Sat, Oct 10th @ 10:24 PM</span><span class=\"answerDetailsSeparator\">|</span><span class=\"timeElpased\">Elapsed: 0:32</span><span class=\"answerResult\"><span style=\"color: green;\">Correct</span></span></div></div>"
    },
    {
      "dom_id": "question-143625",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the following conditional probability density function:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)={\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x, & \\,0\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(X<Y\\,|\\,Y=\\frac{\\pi }{3}).$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that \n\n$$\nP(X\\in A\\,|\\,Y=y)={\\int }_{A}{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ is the conditional probability density function of $X$ given $Y=y.$ \n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<Y\\,|\\,Y=\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & =P(X<\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\,|\\,Y=\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y=\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x]_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [],
      "answer_fields_complete": null,
      "result": "Correct",
      "proof_feedback": null,
