    {
      "dom_id": "question-161606",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}4x\\,\\text{d}V\n$$\n\nover the region $R$ enclosed inside the cylinder ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4$ for $x\\ge 0,$ $y\\ge 0$ and between the surfaces $z=0$ and $z=y+3.$",
      "worked_solution": "We will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,dV={∭}_{Δ}\\,f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,z)\\,r\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta .\n$$\n\nIf $(r,\\theta ,z)$ are the cylindrical polar coordinates of a point, then its Cartesian coordinates $(x,y,z)$ can be found by using the formulas\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,z=z.\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the projection of $R$ onto the $xy$-plane:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14111253/assets/b6bf808437f48af8b0853108079bde0577c92812ebf868d04a0550ecacb3376e.png)\n\nThe region $R$ is a right vertical cylinder of radius $2$ whose axis passes through the point $(0,0)$ in the $xy$-plane, and is\n\n- bounded below by $z=0,$ and\n\n- bounded above by $z=y+3=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +3.$\n\nAs a result, in cylindrical polar coordinates, our region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta ,z)\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 2,\\,0\\le \\theta <\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,0\\le z\\le r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}4x\\,\\text{d}V & ={∭}_{Δ}4r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\cdot r\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +3}4{r}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}4{r}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta [z]_{z=0}^{z=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}4{r}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta (r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +3)\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}4{r}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +12{r}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}2{r}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta +12{r}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{[\\frac{1}{2}{r}^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta +4{r}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ]}_{r=0}^{r=2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{1}{2}(2)^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta +4(2)^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}8\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta +32\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =[-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta +32\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ]_{\\theta =0}^{\\theta =\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-4(-1-1)+32(1-0)) \\\\  & =40.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [],
      "answer_fields_complete": null,
      "result": "Incorrect",
      "proof_feedback": null,
      "html": "<div id=\"question-161606\" class=\"question\"><div class=\"questionHeader\"><span class=\"questionNumber\">19.</span><a class=\"questionKP\" href=\"/topics/2059#12402\">Evaluating a Triple Integral by Converting to Cylindrical Coordinates</a><span class=\"helpButton\" questionid=\"161606\">?</span></div><div class=\"questionText\"><p>Evaluate the triple integral \n<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" display=\"true\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"711\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math display=\"true\" class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"margin-left: 0px; margin-right: 0px;\"><mjx-mstyle><mjx-munder><mjx-row><mjx-base><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-lop\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c222D TEX-S2\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-base></mjx-row><mjx-row><mjx-under style=\"padding-top: 0.167em; padding-left: 0.431em;\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\" size=\"s\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D445 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-under></mjx-row></mjx-munder><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"2\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c34\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D465 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mstyle><mjx-mspace style=\"width: 0.222em;\"></mjx-mspace></mjx-mstyle><mjx-mtext class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c64\"></mjx-c></mjx-mtext><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D449 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-mstyle></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"block\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><munder><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"OP\">∭</mo><mi>R</mi></munder><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\"><mspace width=\"0.222em\"></mspace></mstyle><mtext>d</mtext><mi>V</mi></mstyle></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>\nover the region <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"712\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=