    {
      "dom_id": "question-109869",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Consider a $11\\times 7$ matrix $A.$ If $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}({A}^{T}))=6,$ then $\\text{dim}(\\text{Col}(A))=$",
      "worked_solution": "The four fundamental subspaces of a matrix $A$ can be schematically visualized, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14111253/assets/889b83fadd26b377c4dd34143c9b16541630c04e90de3d9b005e7147ead75ad5.png)\n\nIn our case, we are given that $m=11,$ $n=7,$ and $m-r=6.$ \n\nSubstituting $m=11$ into $m-r=6,$ we can find the rank of $A:$\n\n$$\n(11)-r=6\\,⟹\\,r=5\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{dim}(\\text{Col}(A)) & =r=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [],
      "answer_fields_complete": null,
      "result": "Incorrect",
      "proof_feedback": null,
