      "raw_html": "<div class=\"question\" id=\"question-94377\"><div class=\"questionHeader\"><span class=\"questionNumber\">56.</span><a class=\"questionKP\" href=\"/topics/2526#6733\">Identifying Solutions to Forced Harmonic Motion Equations</a><span class=\"helpButton\" questionid=\"94377\">?</span></div><div class=\"questionText\"><p>A particle is moving with forced harmonic motion without damping. The position of the particle <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"1678\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\"><mjx-math aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"MJX-TEX\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D466 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c28\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D461 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c29\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml display=\"inline\" unselectable=\"on\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> at time <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"1679\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\"><mjx-math aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"MJX-TEX\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D461 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml display=\"inline\" unselectable=\"on\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> is governed by the equation\n<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"1680\" display=\"true\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\"><mjx-math aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"MJX-TEX\" display=\"true\" style=\"margin-left: 0px; margin-right: 0px;\"><mjx-msup><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1