</mspace></mstyle></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> </td><td style=\"text-align:center\"> <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"1991\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\"><mjx-math aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"MJX-TEX\"><mjx-mstyle><mjx-mspace style=\"width: 0.167em;\"></mjx-mspace></mjx-mstyle><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c30\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2E\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c38\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c36\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c38\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c36\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mstyle><mjx-mspace style=\"width: 0.167em;\"></mjx-mspace></mjx-mstyle></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml display=\"inline\" unselectable=\"on\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\"><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace></mstyle><mn>0.8686</mn><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\"><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace></mstyle></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> </td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div><div class=\"answerDetails\"><div class=\"questionDifficulty difficultyEasy\">E</div><span class=\"answerCreated\">Sun, Oct 11th @ 4:29 AM</span><span class=\"answerDetailsSeparator\">|</span><span class=\"timeElpased\">Elapsed: 1:48</span><span class=\"answerResult\"><span style=\"color: green;\">Correct</span></span></div></div>"
    },
    {
      "dom_id": "question-87792",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Solve the inequality $3-2\\sqrt{2x+8}>-9.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we isolate the square root:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3-2\\sqrt{2x+8} & >-9 \\\\ -2\\sqrt{2x+8} & >-12 \\\\ \\sqrt{2x+8} & <6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this inequality, the square root is being compared to a non-negative number $(6).$ So, we can square both sides of the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\sqrt{2x+8})}^{2} & <{6}^{2} \\\\ 2x+8 & <36 \\\\ 2x & <28 \\\\ x & <14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we must only keep the solutions that are in the domain of the square root. To find the domain of the square root, we recall that the argument of the square root must be greater than or equal to zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+8 & \\ge 0 \\\\ 2x & \\ge -8 \\\\ x & \\ge -4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur solution is $x<14,$ which can be expressed as $(-\\infty ,14).$ But the domain of the square root is $x\\ge -4,$ which can be expressed as $[-4,\\infty ).$ To find the solutions that are in the domain of the square root, we take the intersection:\n\n$$\n(-\\infty ,14)\\cap [-4,\\infty )=[-4,14)\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x\\in [-4,14),$ which can also be written as $-4\\le x<14.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [],
      "answer_fields_complete": null,
